---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
import { getRecommendations } from '../lib/content';

// Only quotes with `permission: true` come back. Until Justin confirms written
// permission from each colleague, this is empty and the section says so
// plainly rather than showing placeholder testimonials.
const recommendations = await getRecommendations();
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description={`${site.name} — MBA, University of Denver. Enterprise CX and contact center practitioner in Denver, now building agentic AI environments.`}
>
  <div class="shell pt-14 pb-20 sm:pt-20">
    <p class="annotation">About</p>
    <h1 class="font-display mt-3 max-w-3xl text-3xl font-semibold sm:text-4xl">
      A decade of watching good technology fail for non-technical reasons
    </h1>

    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-14 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_18rem] lg:gap-16">
      <div class="max-w-measure">
        <div class="text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            I've spent my career in and around contact centers — carrying a $30M+ portfolio at
            AT&amp;T, running customer success across three tenures at RingCentral, building an
            enablement function from scratch at Cloud Elements, and owning the Highspot program for
            400+ sellers at Twilio.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-5">
            The pattern that shows up everywhere: the platform was almost never the problem. Someone
            bought good software and then nobody used it the way it was meant to be used, or the
            rollout skipped the part where you find out what people actually do all day. Fixing that
            is unglamorous and it's most of the job.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-5">
            At Northwestern Mutual I rolled out an internal GPT knowledge system to a research team
            of ten, working across internal knowledge bases and compliance documentation. That was
            the first time I saw the same adoption problem play out with AI, and it moved faster and
            cost more when it went wrong.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-5">
            Now at Matrice IT Advisors I build agentic contact center environments on Zoom and
            Dialpad — routing design, API integrations, and the handoff between an agent and a
            human, which is where these deployments are actually judged. I'm Dialpad Agentic
            Delivery Partner certified, and I'm working through Python 3 certification because I'd
            rather read the integration code than be briefed on it.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-5">
            I'm in Denver. I earned my MBA at the University of Denver while working full time,
            which is a slower way to do it and taught me more about prioritization than any of the
            coursework did.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Recommendations -->
        <section class="mt-16" aria-labelledby="recommendations">
          <h2 id="recommendations" class="annotation border-line border-b pb-2">
            What colleagues say
          </h2>

          {
            recommendations.length > 0 ? (
              <ul class="mt-8 grid gap-8">
                {recommendations.map((rec) => (
                  <li>
                    <blockquote class="border-line border-l-2 pl-5">
                      <p class="text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed">{rec.data.quote}</p>
                      <footer class="text-ink-muted mt-3 text-sm">
                        <cite class="not-italic">
                          <span class="text-ink font-medium">{rec.data.name}</span> —{' '}
                          {rec.data.title}, {rec.data.company}
                        </cite>
                      </footer>
                    </blockquote>
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            ) : (
              <p class="text-ink-muted border-line mt-6 border border-dashed p-4 text-sm">
                Nothing here yet. Quotes only appear on this page once the person who wrote them has
                given written permission to publish — the same standard as every other claim on this
                site.
              </p>
            )
          }
        </section>
      </div>

      <!-- Credentials sidebar -->
      <aside class="grid content-start gap-10">
        <div>
          <h2 class="annotation border-line border-b pb-2">Education</h2>
          <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-3 text-sm">
            <li>
              <p class="font-medium">MBA</p>
              <p class="text-ink-muted">University of Denver</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p class="font-medium">BA</p>
              <p class="text-ink-muted">University of Oklahoma</p>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="annotation border-line border-b pb-2">Certifications</h2>
          <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-3 text-sm">
            <li>
              <p class="font-medium">Dialpad Agentic Delivery Partner</p>
              <p class="text-copper text-xs">Certified</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p class="font-medium">Python 3</p>
              <p class="text-ink-muted text-xs">In progress</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p class="font-medium">RingCentral platform</p>
              <p class="text-ink-muted text-xs">In progress</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p class="font-medium">NICE platform</p>
              <p class="text-ink-muted text-xs">In progress</p>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="annotation border-line border-b pb-2">Speaking</h2>
          <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-3 text-sm">
            <li>
              <p class="font-medium">Docebo Inspire 2019</p>
              <p class="text-ink-muted">
                On the seller onboarding and certification program built at Cloud Elements.
              </p>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="border-line border-t pt-6">
          <a href="/resume" class="text-signal text-sm underline underline-offset-4">
            Full resume →
          </a>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
